From: Muthukumar <muthukumardce@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 00:25:32 +0530
Subject: =?UTF-8?q?Fix=20fingerprint=20config=20delivery=20for=20iframes?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20(Site=20Isolation)=20and=0Amulti-RVH=20std::move=20bug?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CommitNavigation() previously sent the session-level fingerprint
overrides to the renderer only when the navigating frame was the main
frame, because the override-config dispatch was inside the same
`if (is main frame) { … }` block as the canvas-noise-token dispatch.
With Site Isolation, a cross-origin iframe commits in a *different
renderer process* than its parent, so the iframe's renderer never
received the config.

The Blink-side override-storage classes that the config feeds —
BatteryManager, UAOverrideManager, NavigatorConcurrentHardware,
ApproximatedDeviceMemory, FontCache and the rest — are all per-process
`static` storage. Without the config push, an iframe's static storage
stays empty and navigator.getBattery(), navigator.userAgent,
navigator.hardwareConcurrency, screen.*, etc. all return the real
system values inside the iframe while the parent frame returns the
spoofed ones. Bot managers (Akamai, Cloudflare, Datadome) that
correlate sensor data across iframes detect the mismatch trivially.

Move the UpdateFingerprintConfig dispatch out of the main-frame
conditional so it runs on every CommitNavigation, regardless of frame
type. Cross-origin subframe commits now push the config to their
renderer process the first time they commit, so their static override
storage is populated before any document JS reads it.

Second, independent bug: inside the ExecutePageBroadcastMethod loop,
the optional fingerprint_config was being `std::move`'d into the call.
ExecutePageBroadcastMethod iterates over every RenderViewHost in the
page broadcast group; the first RVH would consume the moved-from
optional and every subsequent RVH would receive an empty config. Take
a copy ahead of the lambda and pass it by reference so each RVH
iteration sees the full value. (Note `*fingerprint_config` to deref
the optional — we already checked it is engaged.)

Verified on FalconBrowser by loading a page that embeds a cross-origin
iframe and reading navigator.userAgent + navigator.hardwareConcurrency
in both the parent frame and the iframe via DevTools. Before this fix
the iframe returned the real machine's 32 cores and the real Electron
UA; after the fix both frames return the same spoofed values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc
index 94ef5bcaae0b439bfeb9232dde537fe3abdc8b5b..06f89c26c2c21cc3b4eecc5e1d72a9dc69d8547a 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc
@@ -12420,20 +12420,33 @@ void RenderFrameHostImpl::CommitNavigation(
             broadcast->UpdateCanvasNoiseToken(canvas_noise_token);
           }
         });
+  }
 
-    // Send session-level fingerprint overrides to the renderer.
-    // This populates the renderer-side UAOverrideManager so all ForBinding
-    // hooks can read override values directly from C++ storage.
+  // Send session-level fingerprint overrides to the renderer on EVERY frame
+  // commit (main frame AND subframes). With Site Isolation, a cross-origin
+  // iframe commits in a *different renderer process* than its parent. The
+  // override-storage classes in Blink (BatteryManager, UAOverrideManager,
+  // NavigatorConcurrentHardware, ApproximatedDeviceMemory, FontCache, etc.)
+  // are all per-process `static` storage. Without pushing the config to the
+  // iframe's renderer process, its static overrides stay empty and Battery /
+  // UA / screen / hardware APIs return real system values — instantly
+  // inconsistent with the parent frame and trivially detectable by bot
+  // managers that correlate sensor data across iframes.
+  {
     BrowserContext* browser_context =
         frame_tree_node()->navigator().controller().GetBrowserContext();
     auto fingerprint_config =
         GetContentClient()->browser()->GetFingerprintConfig(browser_context);
     if (fingerprint_config) {
+      // Capture by value so each RVH iteration gets its own copy. The previous
+      // implementation moved the optional inside the lambda, leaving every
+      // RVH after the first with an empty config (a second bug independent
+      // from the main-frame-only one above).
+      auto config_to_send = *fingerprint_config;
       frame_tree()->root()->render_manager()->ExecutePageBroadcastMethod(
-          [&fingerprint_config](RenderViewHostImpl* rvh) {
+          [&config_to_send](RenderViewHostImpl* rvh) {
             if (auto& broadcast = rvh->GetAssociatedPageBroadcast()) {
-              broadcast->UpdateFingerprintConfig(
-                  std::move(fingerprint_config));
+              broadcast->UpdateFingerprintConfig(config_to_send);
             }
           });
     }
